quiz.question:
Consider the following Dart code:
```dart
class Animal {
  void eat() {
    print('Eating');
  }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
  void bark() {
    print('Woof!');
  }
}

void main() {
  Dog myDog = Dog();
  myDog.eat(); // Line A
  myDog.bark(); // Line B
}
```
Which statement best describes why `myDog.eat();` (Line A) works?
